{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Braiding.pair_cancellation","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Braiding.pair_cancellation","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Braiding.crossing_energy_channels"],"declarations":1,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.pair_cancellation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.pair_cancellation","kind":"theorem","line":19,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Braiding/pair_cancellation.lean#L19-L31","doc":"**Pair cancellation.** For a composite and its mirror, the symmetric\n(strong) channels cancel and the antisymmetric (Coulomb) channels add:\n\n  `𝔈(𝔥) + 𝔈(𝔥^σ) = 2·E_asym(𝔥)`.\n\nThis is the formal content of the QOU analogue of Einstein's hope for\n`g_[μν]`: the sign-blind antisymmetric sector is what survives when the\nsymmetric sector is cancelled by pairing. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:crossing-energy-pair-cancellation","label":"prop:crossing-energy-pair-cancellation","md":"quantum-observable-universe/observations/crossing-energy-pair-cancellation.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}